    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39352" root="نجب" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُنْجِبٌ</span></b>  A man <i>who begets generous, noble,</i> or
<i>liberal, children; such as are termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نُجَبَاءُ</span>. (K.)
In like manner, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِمْرَأَةٌ مُنْجِبَةٌ</span>, and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِنْجَابٌ</span></b> : (S,
K:) pl. of the latter <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنَاجِيبُ</span>. (S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">منجاب</span></b> 
also signifies A woman <i>who has generous, noble,</i>
or <i>liberal, children; such as are termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نجبآء</span>.
(TA.)

